      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Symptoms like seeing colored streaks or halos often indicate neurological issues such as migraine relatives or retinal problems rather than radiation exposure, since ionizing radiation typically causes immediate tissue damage or cataracts rather than delayed visual phenomena. Have you experienced any headaches, visual distortions during physical exertion, or changes in your eye pressure, as these could suggest a primary vision issue to discuss with a doctor? While the timing of seeing things before an event can be linked to heightened alertness or genuine motion anticipation, the persistent colored mist warrants a professional eye exam to rule out conditions like occipital lobe seizures or specific retinal disorders.",
